steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1784905682
      nanos: 12718354
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "Build a modern SaaS web application called **CaptionDrive**.\n\nThe goal is to help content creators quickly turn images and videos stored in Google Drive into social media-ready posts using AI.\n\nThe application should be simple, fast, and intuitive. It should eliminate the need to search through Google Drive, switch to ChatGPT for captions, and then copy everything into social media.\n\nThe user experience should feel premium, minimal, and AI-first.\n\n---\n\n# Core Problem\n\nCreators have hundreds or thousands of photos and videos in Google Drive.\n\nWhen they want to create a post, they usually:\n\n* Search through folders.\n* Find a photo or video.\n* Download or preview it.\n* Open ChatGPT.\n* Ask for a caption.\n* Rewrite the caption.\n* Copy it into Instagram or LinkedIn.\n\nCaptionDrive should reduce this entire workflow into a few clicks.\n\n---\n\n# Target Users\n\n* Content creators\n* Influencers\n* Small business owners\n* Coaches\n* Freelancers\n* Marketing agencies\n* Social media managers\n\n---\n\n# MVP Features\n\n## 1. User Authentication\n\nAllow users to sign in with:\n\n* Google Sign-In\n\nAfter login, display a simple onboarding flow.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Connect Google Drive\n\nAllow users to securely connect their Google Drive.\n\nRequest read-only access to media files.\n\nThe application should automatically scan for:\n\n* Images\n* Videos\n\nIgnore other file types for the MVP.\n\n---\n\n## 3. AI Media Library\n\nDisplay imported files in a clean, responsive gallery.\n\nEach media card should show:\n\n* Thumbnail\n* File name\n* Upload date\n* File type\n* Folder location\n\nInclude:\n\n* Grid View\n* List View\n* Search by filename\n* Filter by Images or Videos\n* Sort by newest or oldest\n\nClicking a file opens a detailed preview.\n\n---\n\n## 4. AI Content Analysis\n\nWhen a user selects a file, AI should analyze it.\n\n### Images\n\nDetect:\n\n* Main subject\n* Objects\n* Scene\n* Mood\n* Colors\n* Activities\n* Overall context\n\nGenerate a short summary describing the image.\n\n### Videos\n\nGenerate:\n\n* Speech transcript (if available)\n* Video summary\n* Main topic\n* Key talking points\n* Suggested thumbnail timestamp\n\nDisplay all AI insights in a clean side panel.\n\n---\n\n## 5. AI Caption Generator\n\nAllow users to generate captions based on the selected media.\n\nProvide caption styles such as:\n\n* Storytelling\n* Educational\n* Promotional\n* Inspirational\n* Professional\n* Casual\n* Humorous\n\nEach generated result should include:\n\n* Hook\n* Main caption\n* Call-to-action\n* Relevant hashtags\n\nGenerate three different caption variations so users can choose the one they like best.\n\nInclude buttons for:\n\n* Copy Caption\n* Regenerate\n* Edit Caption\n\n---\n\n## 6. Caption Settings\n\nBefore generating captions, allow users to choose:\n\nPlatform:\n\n* Instagram\n* LinkedIn\n* Facebook\n* X\n\nTone:\n\n* Professional\n* Friendly\n* Funny\n* Luxury\n* Inspirational\n\nCaption Length:\n\n* Short\n* Medium\n* Long\n\nTarget Audience:\n\n* Business owners\n* Entrepreneurs\n* Students\n* Creators\n* General audience\n\nThese preferences should influence the AI output.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Smart Search (Premium Feature)\n\nAllow users to search their media library using natural language.\n\nExamples:\n\n\"Show my beach photos.\"\n\n\"Find videos about AI.\"\n\n\"Find pictures with laptops.\"\n\n\"Show speaking event photos.\"\n\nThe AI should search based on the visual content, not just filenames.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Favorite Media\n\nAllow users to save files as Favorites for quick access.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Recent Captions\n\nMaintain a history of previously generated captions.\n\nAllow users to:\n\n* View\n* Copy\n* Delete\n\n---\n\n## User Interface\n\nThe design should be modern and minimalist.\n\nInspired by:\n\n* ChatGPT\n* Notion\n* Linear\n* Dropbox\n* Google Photos\n\nThe interface should use:\n\n* Rounded cards\n* Plenty of white space\n* Smooth animations\n* Responsive layouts\n* Dark and Light mode\n* Drag-and-drop interactions where appropriate\n\n---\n\n## Navigation\n\nSidebar:\n\n* Dashboard\n* My Media\n* Favorites\n* Recent Captions\n* Settings\n\nMain Dashboard:\n\n* Recently imported files\n* Quick caption generator\n* Recent activity\n\n---\n\n## Future Features (Design the architecture to support them, but do not build them yet)\n\n* Brand Voice learning\n* Auto-posting to social media\n* Content calendar\n* Scheduled publishing\n* Analytics dashboard\n* AI content recommendations\n* Team collaboration\n* Dropbox integration\n* OneDrive integration\n* Google Photos integration\n\n---\n\n## Suggested Tech Stack\n\nFrontend:\n\n* Next.js\n* React\n* TypeScript\n* Tailwind CSS\n* shadcn/ui\n\nBackend:\n\n* Supabase\n* PostgreSQL\n* Supabase Authentication\n* Supabase Storage\n\nAI:\n\n* OpenAI GPT for caption generation\n* Vision model for image understanding\n* Whisper for video transcription\n\nIntegrations:\n\n* Google OAuth\n* Google Drive API\n\n---\n\n## Database Structure\n\nUsers\n\n* id\n* name\n* email\n* avatar\n\nMedia\n\n* id\n* user_id\n* drive_file_id\n* filename\n* file_type\n* thumbnail\n* folder\n* uploaded_at\n* ai_summary\n\nCaptions\n\n* id\n* media_id\n* platform\n* tone\n* length\n* caption\n* hashtags\n* created_at\n\nFavorites\n\n* user_id\n* media_id\n\n---\n\n## Success Criteria\n\nThe application should allow a creator to:\n\n1. Sign in with Google.\n2. Connect Google Drive.\n3. Browse their images and videos.\n4. Select a file.\n5. Have AI understand the content.\n6. Generate three high-quality captions tailored to a chosen platform and tone.\n7. Copy a caption and publish it manually.\n\nThe entire workflow should take less than one minute and feel seamless, making CaptionDrive the fastest way to turn Google Drive media into engaging social media posts.\n"
    items {
      text: "Build a modern SaaS web application called **CaptionDrive**.\n\nThe goal is to help content creators quickly turn images and videos stored in Google Drive into social media-ready posts using AI.\n\nThe application should be simple, fast, and intuitive. It should eliminate the need to search through Google Drive, switch to ChatGPT for captions, and then copy everything into social media.\n\nThe user experience should feel premium, minimal, and AI-first.\n\n---\n\n# Core Problem\n\nCreators have hundreds or thousands of photos and videos in Google Drive.\n\nWhen they want to create a post, they usually:\n\n* Search through folders.\n* Find a photo or video.\n* Download or preview it.\n* Open ChatGPT.\n* Ask for a caption.\n* Rewrite the caption.\n* Copy it into Instagram or LinkedIn.\n\nCaptionDrive should reduce this entire workflow into a few clicks.\n\n---\n\n# Target Users\n\n* Content creators\n* Influencers\n* Small business owners\n* Coaches\n* Freelancers\n* Marketing agencies\n* Social media managers\n\n---\n\n# MVP Features\n\n## 1. User Authentication\n\nAllow users to sign in with:\n\n* Google Sign-In\n\nAfter login, display a simple onboarding flow.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Connect Google Drive\n\nAllow users to securely connect their Google Drive.\n\nRequest read-only access to media files.\n\nThe application should automatically scan for:\n\n* Images\n* Videos\n\nIgnore other file types for the MVP.\n\n---\n\n## 3. AI Media Library\n\nDisplay imported files in a clean, responsive gallery.\n\nEach media card should show:\n\n* Thumbnail\n* File name\n* Upload date\n* File type\n* Folder location\n\nInclude:\n\n* Grid View\n* List View\n* Search by filename\n* Filter by Images or Videos\n* Sort by newest or oldest\n\nClicking a file opens a detailed preview.\n\n---\n\n## 4. AI Content Analysis\n\nWhen a user selects a file, AI should analyze it.\n\n### Images\n\nDetect:\n\n* Main subject\n* Objects\n* Scene\n* Mood\n* Colors\n* Activities\n* Overall context\n\nGenerate a short summary describing the image.\n\n### Videos\n\nGenerate:\n\n* Speech transcript (if available)\n* Video summary\n* Main topic\n* Key talking points\n* Suggested thumbnail timestamp\n\nDisplay all AI insights in a clean side panel.\n\n---\n\n## 5. AI Caption Generator\n\nAllow users to generate captions based on the selected media.\n\nProvide caption styles such as:\n\n* Storytelling\n* Educational\n* Promotional\n* Inspirational\n* Professional\n* Casual\n* Humorous\n\nEach generated result should include:\n\n* Hook\n* Main caption\n* Call-to-action\n* Relevant hashtags\n\nGenerate three different caption variations so users can choose the one they like best.\n\nInclude buttons for:\n\n* Copy Caption\n* Regenerate\n* Edit Caption\n\n---\n\n## 6. Caption Settings\n\nBefore generating captions, allow users to choose:\n\nPlatform:\n\n* Instagram\n* LinkedIn\n* Facebook\n* X\n\nTone:\n\n* Professional\n* Friendly\n* Funny\n* Luxury\n* Inspirational\n\nCaption Length:\n\n* Short\n* Medium\n* Long\n\nTarget Audience:\n\n* Business owners\n* Entrepreneurs\n* Students\n* Creators\n* General audience\n\nThese preferences should influence the AI output.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Smart Search (Premium Feature)\n\nAllow users to search their media library using natural language.\n\nExamples:\n\n\"Show my beach photos.\"\n\n\"Find videos about AI.\"\n\n\"Find pictures with laptops.\"\n\n\"Show speaking event photos.\"\n\nThe AI should search based on the visual content, not just filenames.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Favorite Media\n\nAllow users to save files as Favorites for quick access.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Recent Captions\n\nMaintain a history of previously generated captions.\n\nAllow users to:\n\n* View\n* Copy\n* Delete\n\n---\n\n## User Interface\n\nThe design should be modern and minimalist.\n\nInspired by:\n\n* ChatGPT\n* Notion\n* Linear\n* Dropbox\n* Google Photos\n\nThe interface should use:\n\n* Rounded cards\n* Plenty of white space\n* Smooth animations\n* Responsive layouts\n* Dark and Light mode\n* Drag-and-drop interactions where appropriate\n\n---\n\n## Navigation\n\nSidebar:\n\n* Dashboard\n* My Media\n* Favorites\n* Recent Captions\n* Settings\n\nMain Dashboard:\n\n* Recently imported files\n* Quick caption generator\n* Recent activity\n\n---\n\n## Future Features (Design the architecture to support them, but do not build them yet)\n\n* Brand Voice learning\n* Auto-posting to social media\n* Content calendar\n* Scheduled publishing\n* Analytics dashboard\n* AI content recommendations\n* Team collaboration\n* Dropbox integration\n* OneDrive integration\n* Google Photos integration\n\n---\n\n## Suggested Tech Stack\n\nFrontend:\n\n* Next.js\n* React\n* TypeScript\n* Tailwind CSS\n* shadcn/ui\n\nBackend:\n\n* Supabase\n* PostgreSQL\n* Supabase Authentication\n* Supabase Storage\n\nAI:\n\n* OpenAI GPT for caption generation\n* Vision model for image understanding\n* Whisper for video transcription\n\nIntegrations:\n\n* Google OAuth\n* Google Drive API\n\n---\n\n## Database Structure\n\nUsers\n\n* id\n* name\n* email\n* avatar\n\nMedia\n\n* id\n* user_id\n* drive_file_id\n* filename\n* file_type\n* thumbnail\n* folder\n* uploaded_at\n* ai_summary\n\nCaptions\n\n* id\n* media_id\n* platform\n* tone\n* length\n* caption\n* hashtags\n* created_at\n\nFavorites\n\n* user_id\n* media_id\n\n---\n\n## Success Criteria\n\nThe application should allow a creator to:\n\n1. Sign in with Google.\n2. Connect Google Drive.\n3. Browse their images and videos.\n4. Select a file.\n5. Have AI understand the content.\n6. Generate three high-quality captions tailored to a chosen platform and tone.\n7. Copy a caption and publish it manually.\n\nThe entire workflow should take less than one minute and feel seamless, making CaptionDrive the fastest way to turn Google Drive media into engaging social media posts.\n"
    }
  }
