  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Core Structure**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the fundamental architecture of CaptionDrive. I\'m focusing on a full-stack Express, Vite, and React application, aiming for a setup on port 3000. Right now, I\'m reviewing the best practice setup guidelines for full-stack apps. I\'m checking the recommended dev script configuration for `server.ts` within the package.json file.\n\n\n**Evaluating Package Dependencies**\n\nI\'m now investigating package dependencies, particularly for Google Drive API interaction. I\'m leaning toward using the `googleapis` library for its robustness in handling the Google Drive API. I\'m weighing this against the option of using `fetch` directly with Google API endpoints. I\'m also considering `cookie-parser` or `express-session` for token management if necessary. I\'ve noted OAuth configuration will be handled using system environment variables from AI Studio.\n\n\n**Assessing OAuth Integration**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on integrating Google OAuth for CaptionDrive, and evaluating different approaches for handling authorization in the AI Studio environment. I\'m investigating how the AI Studio handles OAuth sign-in flow and also a direct sign-in method with simulated Google Drive scanning using the Google Drive REST API. I\'m thinking about including endpoints for Google OAuth authorization URLs, callbacks, and file fetching, which would cover both real OAuth integration and a demo mode.\n\n\n**Defining API Endpoints**\n\nI\'m now concretizing the API endpoints in `server.ts`. I need `/api/auth/me` to get user session state, `/api/auth/google/login` to start Google sign-in. There\'s an `/api/drive/files` endpoint, which is used for the retrieval of Drive files, with specific fields. And I\'m also planning for endpoints that can handle Google Drive account disconnect and re-connection. I\'ve designed a demo mode with sample media for quick evaluation.\n\n\n**Expanding API Functionality**\n\nI\'m now adding logout functionality with `/api/auth/logout` to clear the session. I\'m also adding `/api/drive/connect` for the Google OAuth connection. The `/api/drive/files` endpoint, will scan files from Google Drive or our local state. Finally, I\'m working on the AI integration. I\'ll need to use `@google/genai` (Gemini) to analyze media via `/api/ai/analyze`, and generate captions via `/api/ai/generate-captions`.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 366748037
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
