  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Structuring the application**\n\nI\'ve successfully installed `googleapis`! Currently, I\'m carefully organizing the application\'s file structure. I\'m focusing on defining Types and Models within the `/src/types.ts` file, and I\'ve started the TypeScript definitions for User, DriveFile, MediaItem, AICaptionRequest, AICaptionResult, CaptionVariation, CaptionSettings, CaptionHistoryItem, FilterState, and View.\n\n\n**Defining Server and Data**\n\nI\'m now diving into the server and data aspects. I\'m working on `/src/data/sampleDriveMedia.ts`, crafting rich sample media with realistic image URLs and videos to allow immediate testing. Concurrently, I\'m setting up a custom Express server in `/server.ts` to handle Google Drive OAuth and the Gemini API, ensuring secure storage of user data, preferences, and caption history. I\'m also planning the AI analysis endpoint with Gemini\'s vision capabilities and the tailored caption generator.\n\n\n**Designing the User Interface**\n\nI\'m now deeply immersed in the UI component architecture, and I am excited by how it\'s shaping up. I\'m focusing on user needs, especially for media management. I am developing `Navbar`, `Sidebar`, `OnboardingModal`, `ConnectDriveBanner`, `MediaGrid`, and `MediaDetailModal` components in `/src/components`. I\'m prioritizing user experience with features like theme toggle, Google Drive integration, a media grid view, and a user-friendly onboarding experience. I plan to use history management endpoints.\n\n\n**Refining the Media View**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the media view. I\'m focused on high-resolution previews for both images and videos. I\'m building out the AI Content Analysis panel to provide users with insights like detected subjects, objects, mood, and scene. I\'m also adding an interactive \"Generate Caption\" trigger to begin the caption process. I\'m now implementing the caption generator modal, including the settings bar for platform, tone, length, and audience. I\'m focusing on user control. I plan realistic loading animations!\n\n\n**Expanding the Views**\n\nI\'m now expanding the application\'s core views. I am developing a `CaptionHistoryView` with filters, search, copy, and delete options, and a `FavoritesView` for starred media. Additionally, I\'m working on a comprehensive `DashboardView` with stats, quick caption workflow, and recent activity. I\'m also preparing a `SettingsView` for account and preference management. I\'ve updated the `package.json` scripts.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 470470697
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
