    thinking: "**Building React Components**\n\nI\'ve got the `server.ts` file in place. Now, I\'m diving into the React components. I\'m focusing on a clean hierarchy. My initial plan involves a `/src/components/Navbar.tsx` file to get started, with the design elements like the app logo, a search bar, and Google Drive integration, so I can start from there.\n\n\n**Defining UI Components**\n\nOkay, I\'m now structuring the remaining React components. I\'m moving on to building out the `Sidebar.tsx` file, with navigation items, a quick stats widget, and a connection button. I\'m also thinking about a banner component (`ConnectDriveBanner.tsx`) to show the Google Drive status. Next, I plan to focus on the `MediaCard.tsx` component, the core element for displaying individual media.\n\n\n**Designing Interactive Modals**\n\nI\'m now focusing on interactive modals. I\'m building a detailed `MediaDetailModal.tsx` for displaying media with an image/video viewer and an AI Content Analysis drawer. This includes features like \"Generate Captions.\" The `CaptionGeneratorModal.tsx` is also in progress. I\'m designing a workbench with platform/tone/length selectors, a target audience option, and a custom notes textarea to make the whole process easier. I\'m planning to use a \"Generate 3 Captions with Gemini AI\" button with an animated state, showing output variations.\n\n\n**Constructing Core Views**\n\nI\'m now building the core views. I\'m focusing on `/src/components/DashboardView.tsx`, with a creator greeting, overview metrics, quick action banner, and recently synced media. I\'m also thinking about adding generated captions. I\'ve designed the `/src/components/FavoritesView.tsx` with quick filters and caption generation and `/src/components/CaptionHistoryView.tsx` with a timeline and platform filters. Finally, I\'m working on `/src/components/SettingsView.tsx` with user profile, Google account settings and default caption preferences.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
