  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Adding Social Endpoints**\n\nI\'ve begun implementing social media endpoints within `server.ts`. Currently, I\'m working on the `/api/social/accounts` GET endpoint to retrieve stored social media accounts. Next, I\'ll be focused on POST endpoints, handling account addition and auto-posting features with user approval. The structure will be similar to other features, with the same modularity.\n\n\n**Implementing Disconnect Logic**\n\nI\'ve just added the `/connect` endpoint, which handles connecting social accounts, updating existing ones, or creating new entries in `socialAccountsStore`. I also integrated a disconnect endpoint, making it possible to mark accounts as disconnected. I\'ve designed a clear structure for handling social account connections.\n\n\n**Finalizing Publish Functionality**\n\nI\'ve just finished the `/api/social/posts` and `/api/social/publish` endpoints. The publishing endpoint includes validations. Posts require user approval to be scheduled or sent. I added placeholder URLs for various platforms. I have also implemented the GET endpoint to list the posts. I\'m now testing the publishing workflow to verify it functions as intended.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 833123423
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
