    thinking: "**Pinpointing the Trigger**\n\nI\'ve discovered something crucial: the `variations` array is initialized empty (`[]`) when the `CaptionGeneratorModal` opens. Importantly, the `handleGenerateCaptions` function isn\'t being called automatically upon modal mount! This means \"Generate Captions\" or modal opening *alone* doesn\'t trigger the Gemini generation unless the user explicitly clicks the \"Generate Captions with Gemini\" button.\n\n\n**Automating Caption Generation**\n\nI\'m now implementing an `useEffect` hook within `CaptionGeneratorModal.tsx` to automatically trigger `handleGenerateCaptions()` upon modal mount. This aims to prevent user confusion by immediately generating captions when the modal opens, instead of requiring an extra click. I\'m also ensuring easy regeneration with a button or after tweaking settings. Concurrently, I\'m working to make the backend caption generation more reliable with clean JSON extraction, a specific MIME type, and smart fallback mechanisms in `server.ts`.\n\n\n"
