    thinking: "**Analyzing Dark Mode Implementation**\n\nI\'m currently reviewing how the dark mode is implemented in the application, specifically focusing on lines 64-70 in `src/App.tsx`. I see the `useEffect` hook is managing the addition and removal of the \'dark\' class to the document root based on the `darkMode` state. My focus is now on the CSS side to ensure a full understanding of the visual changes triggered by this class toggle.\n\n\n**Investigating Tailwind CSS v4**\n\nI\'m digging deeper into how Tailwind CSS handles dark mode, particularly in v4. I\'ve realized the initial implementation is likely using the older version, given the `@import \"tailwindcss\";` directive in `src/index.css`. This is leading me to explore class-based dark mode configurations and how the `dark:` variants function in this context. I\'m trying to see if there\'s a disconnect between how the class is being toggled and how Tailwind is interpreting it. I see that `prefers-color-scheme: dark` has not been set, and I am exploring possible causes.\n\n\n"
