    thinking: "**Defining Global Styles**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining global styles, specifically aiming for custom properties and clean tokens within `index.css`. This is the foundational layer, and I\'m strategizing how to establish a consistent visual language that resonates with the desired Kickpush agency aesthetic.\n\n\n**Establishing Theme Elements**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on theme specifics. I\'ve pinned down light and dark mode colors for background and text, including off-white/charcoal and obsidian/crisp warm variations. I\'ve also solidified our Kickpush Vermillion accent color and neutral border colors. I\'m keen to eliminate those generic blues, preferring to use our bold accent or high-contrast obsidian button styles instead. I\'m also planning for smooth transitions.\n\n\n**Designing Interface Details**\n\nI\'m now integrating crucial interface elements. I\'ve designed a bold \"Upload Content\" button with a striking visual signature for both light and dark modes. I\'m also including a crisp, minimal dark mode toggle icon. The sidebar will have a minimalist editorial design with a \"WORKSPACE // CREATIVE\" section label, nav items with refined icons and hover states, and a Google Drive sync status box. Finally, I\'m transforming the dashboard into a bold, editorial workspace with a large headline greeting and asymmetrical layout.\n\n\n**Integrating Content Actions**\n\nI\'m now integrating crucial content actions. I\'m focusing on \"Content Waiting for Captions\" with a media grid, each item having thumbnail, duration, AI analysis tag, and a direct \"Generate Caption\" action. I\'m also including \"Recent Generated Captions\" as clean cards with hook, body preview, platform tag, copy button, and publish trigger, plus an \"Upcoming Posts & Schedule\" minimal queue, and quick actions as mono-styled tags. I\'m also developing the content library with large visual media previews, minimalist card overlays, and folder tabs.\n\n\n**Developing Caption Studio**\n\nI\'m now deep in the AI Caption Studio. I\'ve designed a split workspace with a large media canvas on the left, integrating AI visual analysis, and a creative writing engine on the right. I\'m focusing on dynamic AI prompt tweaks within the \"Regenerate\" button to improve AI-powered generation. I\'m building controls for tone, platform, length, and target audience, all leading to a live caption preview with copy, save, and publish actions.\n\n\n"
